## Summary

Closes #20248

`exhaustive-deps` already detects this case:

```js
function f() {
  const unstable = [];
  useMemo(() => unstable, [unstable]);
}
```

but not this case:

```js
function f({ unstable = [] }) {
  useMemo(() => unstable, [unstable]);
}
```

nor this case:

```js
function f(unstable = []) {
  useMemo(() => unstable, [unstable]);
}
```

This PR makes the rule detect both of these new cases. 

